From 164bb95ed12ebdb690500f97585c25c1adc01c89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:09:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: without the refresh rate adjustment, the Dolby
 Vision size after the first file too

With "adjust display refresh rate" off, Hades changes only the size of
the mode: to the 3840x2160 mode at the same rate that native Dolby
Vision output needs (a GUI at 1080p), and back to the GUI mode for a
following stream without it. CVideoPlayer::OpenVideoStream() makes that
choice in the block that sets the mode of a first file, under
m_CurrentVideo.id < 0.

A file that is opened while another still plays (the user skips to the
next item or picks another one) keeps the open video stream: the block
is not for it, and with the adjustment off nothing else chooses. Its
Dolby Vision went out on the ordinary output, or the 3840x2160 mode of
the file before stayed for a file without it. The same held for a
video that went to full screen after it had started. (At the natural
end of a file the player's thread ends, and the next item of a playlist
is opened as a first file: that case was right already. Three comments
that said "the next file of a playlist" now say which one.)

The choice is now also made in CRenderManager::UpdateResolution(), the
place where the mode is chosen with the adjustment on: after a renderer
is configured, when the frame rate changes, when the video goes to full
screen. It runs on the application thread, as every other change of
mode there; it is not made from the player thread, which the
application thread may be waiting for (a stop) while a synchronous
request to it would wait for the application thread. A renderer that
was configured in a mode that cannot carry the transport does not ask
for native output and captures nothing; it is configured again once
the mode can (DVBridgeConfigChanged()), so the output is not turned
off and on for this.

Between a file and the next one the intent kept by the render manager
is neither's: it is cleared when the new file starts, and the video
stream of the new file sets it some time later. A choice made in
between (the user goes to the GUI and back) would have taken a Dolby
Vision file for one without, gone back to the GUI mode and returned.
The render manager now keeps the intent as one value that also says
"not known yet" (m_nativeDVIntent: cleared by NewFile(), which is the
first thing a new file does, set by SetNativeDVStream()), read once
for this choice, and the choice waits, with its trigger, until the
video stream has said it. For a file without video it waits for the
whole file, which leaves the mode where it was, as before.

For a first file nothing changes: its mode is already the one this
would choose. With the adjustment on, this code is not reached, and
the mode is chosen as before (also in that gap, with the cleared
intent).

Not covered: a file opened while another plays whose pictures need no
new renderer and no other frame rate, and that does not go to full
screen anew, asks for no choice at all (a Dolby Vision file after one
that could not have native output, with the same picture parameters):
it stays on the ordinary output, as before. And the rule that goes
back to the GUI mode cannot tell whose 3840x2160 mode it undoes
(comment in Resolution.cpp).

Read in the code, reviewed, and read again after its corrections; it
cannot be run in a host test, and has not been seen on a display.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp        | 13 +++---
 .../VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp          | 43 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../VideoRenderers/RenderManager.h            | 18 ++++++--
 xbmc/windowing/Resolution.cpp                 |  5 ++-
 4 files changed, 68 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
index 149c14f..6401608 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -1464,10 +1464,12 @@ void CVideoPlayer::Prepare()
 #ifdef HAVE_DVBRIDGE
   // a new video, before its input and streams open: the display is looked at again and, when it
   // changed, native Dolby Vision output disabled by a failure is tried with it (never during a
-  // video); the Dolby Vision intent of the previous file is gone (the next file of a playlist
-  // reuses this player without closing its video stream)
+  // video). The Dolby Vision intent of the previous file went with NewFile() above, and the
+  // one of this file is not known until its video stream opens (a file that is opened while
+  // another still plays reuses this player without closing its video stream; at the natural
+  // end of a file the player's thread ends, and the next item of a playlist is opened as a
+  // first file)
   DVBRIDGE::NewVideo();
-  m_renderManager.SetNativeDVStream(false);
   m_dvNewFile = true;
 #endif
   CFFmpegLog::SetLogLevel(1);
@@ -4566,8 +4568,9 @@ bool CVideoPlayer::OpenVideoStream(CDVDStreamInfo& hint, bool reset)
   if (m_CurrentVideo.id < 0 || m_dvNewFile)
   {
     // for native Dolby Vision output in a transport mode, whatever the current mode; the mode
-    // chosen for the stream holds for the whole stream. Also for the first video stream of the
-    // next file of a playlist, which reuses the open video stream (m_CurrentVideo.id >= 0).
+    // chosen for the stream holds for the whole stream. Also for the first video stream of a
+    // file that is opened while another still plays, which reuses the open video stream
+    // (m_CurrentVideo.id >= 0).
     m_dvNewFile = false;
     nativeDV = DVBRIDGE::WantsNativeOutputMode(hint);
     m_renderManager.SetNativeDVStream(nativeDV);
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
index fc1b125..79f0d47 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
@@ -156,10 +156,16 @@ bool CRenderManager::Configure(const VideoPicture& picture,
 #ifdef HAVE_DVBRIDGE
     // A native stream keeps its display mode for the whole stream: pictures that lose their Dolby
     // Vision metadata (the ordinary output, until it comes back) must not switch the mode during
-    // playback. VideoPlayer sets it when the stream opens and UnInit() clears it; a picture with
-    // metadata only adds to it.
+    // playback. VideoPlayer sets it when the stream opens, UnInit() and NewFile() clear it; a
+    // picture with metadata only adds to it.
     if (DVBRIDGE::WantsNativeOutputMode(&picture))
+    {
       m_nativeDVRate = true;
+      // (raised only from what the stream said: a late picture of the file before does not
+      // make the intent of a new file known)
+      int no = 0;
+      m_nativeDVIntent.compare_exchange_strong(no, 1);
+    }
 #endif
     m_fps = fps;
     UpdateProgressive(progressive);
@@ -436,6 +442,7 @@ void CRenderManager::UnInit()
 
   m_renderState = STATE_UNCONFIGURED;
   m_picture.Reset();
+  m_nativeDVIntent = -1;
   m_nativeDVRate = false;
   m_progressive = false;
   m_progressiveSet = false;
@@ -881,6 +888,35 @@ void CRenderManager::UpdateResolution()
         if (m_pRenderer)
           m_pRenderer->Update();
       }
+#ifdef HAVE_DVBRIDGE
+      else if (CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent()->GetSettings()->GetInt(
+                   CSettings::SETTING_VIDEOPLAYER_ADJUSTREFRESHRATE) == ADJUST_REFRESHRATE_OFF)
+      {
+        // Hades: without the adjustment of the refresh rate only the size changes: to the
+        // 3840x2160 mode at the same rate that native Dolby Vision output needs, and back.
+        // VideoPlayer chooses it when the stream of a first file opens. A file that is
+        // opened while another still plays keeps the open video stream, and a video may go
+        // to full screen after it started: nothing chose for those. Here, where the mode is
+        // chosen with the adjustment, the same choice is made for them. A renderer that was
+        // configured in a mode that cannot carry the transport is configured again once the
+        // mode can (CLinuxRendererGLES::DVBridgeConfigChanged()).
+        // Between a file and the next one the intent is the cleared one of neither: the
+        // choice waits, with its trigger, until the video stream of the new file has said
+        // its own (for the whole of a file that has no video).
+        const int intent = m_nativeDVIntent;
+        if (intent < 0)
+          return;
+        auto& gfx = CServiceBroker::GetWinSystem()->GetGfxContext();
+        const RESOLUTION res = CResolutionUtils::ChooseDVResolutionWithoutAdjustment(intent > 0);
+        if (res != gfx.GetVideoResolution())
+        {
+          gfx.SetVideoResolution(res, false);
+          UpdateLatencyTweak();
+          if (m_pRenderer)
+            m_pRenderer->Update();
+        }
+      }
+#endif
       m_bTriggerUpdateResolution = false;
       m_playerPort->VideoParamsChange();
     }
@@ -894,6 +930,7 @@ void CRenderManager::TriggerUpdateResolution(float fps, int width, int height, s
   {
     // The stream's intent (native Dolby Vision), as SetNativeDVStream() sets it.
     m_nativeDVRate = nativeDV;
+    m_nativeDVIntent = nativeDV ? 1 : 0;
     UpdateProgressive(progressive);
     m_fps = fps;
     m_picture.iWidth = width;
@@ -907,6 +944,8 @@ void CRenderManager::NewFile()
 {
   m_progressiveSet = false;
   m_fileModeChosen = false;
+  m_nativeDVIntent = -1;
+  m_nativeDVRate = false;
 }
 
 bool CRenderManager::UpdateProgressive(bool progressive)
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.h
index 2c3cfd0..f85fb5d 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.h
@@ -82,10 +82,18 @@ public:
                                bool nativeDV = false, bool progressive = false);
   //! A new stream is for native Dolby Vision output: its display mode is a transport mode for
   //! the whole stream (see Configure()).
-  void SetNativeDVStream(bool nativeDV) { m_nativeDVRate = nativeDV; }
-  //! A new file starts (VideoPlayer, before its streams open; the next file of a playlist reuses the
-  //! video stream): its first stream or picture sets whether it is progressive again, and its first
+  void SetNativeDVStream(bool nativeDV)
+  {
+    m_nativeDVRate = nativeDV;
+    m_nativeDVIntent = nativeDV ? 1 : 0;
+  }
+  //! A new file starts (VideoPlayer, before its streams open; a file that is opened while another
+  //! still plays reuses the video stream): its first stream or picture sets whether it is
+  //! progressive again, and its first
   //! choice of display mode is free again (see UpdateProgressive() and UpdateResolution()).
+  //! Hades: the Dolby Vision intent of the file before is gone with it, and the one of this file
+  //! is not known until its video stream opens (SetNativeDVStream()): until then the size that
+  //! is chosen without the adjustment of the refresh rate is not chosen (UpdateResolution()).
   void NewFile();
   void SetViewMode(int iViewMode);
   void PreInit();
@@ -185,6 +193,10 @@ protected:
   CCriticalSection m_datalock;
   bool m_bTriggerUpdateResolution = false;
   std::atomic_bool m_nativeDVRate{false};
+  //! Hades: m_nativeDVRate as the stream of the current file said it (0 or 1), or -1 while it
+  //! has not: one value, read once, for the choice that must not be made with the intent of
+  //! the file before
+  std::atomic_int m_nativeDVIntent{-1};
   //! the stream may get a half refresh rate (see CResolutionUtils::ChooseBestResolution())
   std::atomic_bool m_progressive{false};
   //! m_progressive was set for the current file
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/Resolution.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/Resolution.cpp
index cb46eb1..4731ef4 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/Resolution.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/Resolution.cpp
@@ -167,7 +167,10 @@ RESOLUTION CResolutionUtils::ChooseDVResolutionWithoutAdjustment(bool nativeDV)
   // The GUI mode, as CGraphicContext::SetFullScreenVideo() restores it when playback stops. Kodi
   // stays in the full-screen video window between the items of a playlist, so a 3840x2160 mode
   // chosen for an earlier native stream in place of the GUI mode would stay; nothing else
-  // changes the mode without the adjustment, and only that change is undone.
+  // changes the mode without the adjustment, and that change is undone. (The rule cannot tell
+  // whose mode it is: a 3840x2160 mode at the rate of the GUI mode that the adjustment chose,
+  // before the user turned it off during playback or with the "on start" setting that does
+  // not go back at a stop, goes back to the GUI mode as well.)
   RESOLUTION gui = RES_DESKTOP;
   if (CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetCurrentResolution() > RES_DESKTOP)
     gui = CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetCurrentResolution();
-- 
